2026-11-19 20:51:21 - Agent_20261119205029 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed the requests 2.19.0 redirect-credential group. Confirmed CVE-2018-18074: rebuild_auth (requests/sessions.py:239-250) strips the Authorization header only when the hostname changes, so an https->http downgrade (or hostname-equal, different-port redirect) leaks the auth header in clear text. Submitted the vulnerable comparison at line 250 and the strip-decision context at line 239 as true positives (one result, lines 239/250, plus the line-245 preparation recognized as part of it). Classified the informational pan-group results as false positives: rebuild_proxies always deletes and rebuilds Proxy-Authorization from the newly-resolved proxy URL (sessions.py:283-292), and auth.py/adapters.py header literals are intended credential attachment. Recommended remediation: compare scheme and port as in 2.20.0's should_strip_auth.
