2026-11-19 20:52:52 - Agent_20261119205029 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed both results from py/requests-final-tls-sweep in requests/__init__.py.

Line 106: `warnings.simplefilter('ignore', DependencyWarning)` — this suppresses only urllib3's `DependencyWarning` class (version/pyOpenSSL dependency mismatch notifications). It does not mute `InsecureRequestWarning`, `SNIMissingWarning`, or `SecurityWarning`, which are the classes urllib3 emits for disabled TLS verification. Verified via grep that no TLS-related warning class is filtered anywhere in requests/ (only tests filter SNIMissingWarning for test hygiene).

Line 136: `warnings.simplefilter('default', FileModeWarning, append=True)` — explicitly sets FileModeWarning to be *shown* (default level), the opposite of muting. FileModeWarning relates to opening files in binary vs text mode, unrelated to TLS.

Both are false positives for CWE-295/CWE-522. The only residual observation is that these calls mutate the process-wide warnings filter at import time (a global side effect), but this does not weaken TLS security signaling, so neither warrants a vulnerability finding.
